{"clock":1,"nonce":"4c2aedf408c2b42e3382d8bfe1627e43","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793807403,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6206257458"},"data":{"body":"Follow-up of #76 (PR #81).\n\n**Now.** A board kept in Markdown files (`board.datastore markdown:\u003cdir\u003e`) or on the forges alone has no counter: its issues go by the forges' numbers, files are named by the id's first 7 digits, and Settings › Numbers says the datastore keeps none. Git keeps `refs/board/seq` on origin; PostgreSQL a row.\n\n**Question first.** A Markdown board's files merge across branches (git's union driver on `.board/*.jsonl`). A counter file can't merge that way: two branches numbering at once would give one number twice. Options:\n- **A. Number on the default branch only**: `.board/numbers` written only when the checkout is on it, a merge from a branch keeps the default branch's. Simple; issues made on a branch wait for the merge.\n- **B. Numbers from the forge** the board syncs with (GitHub's): no counter of our own, the number the forge gave. Already the case for linked issues.\n- **C. No numbers on Markdown boards**, said in the docs (today).\n\n**Want (if A).** `mdstore` implements `datastore.Counter` over `.board/numbers` (the same file format as `refs/board/seq`), refusing to write off the default branch with a sentence; `internal/store` numbers through it as for PostgreSQL.\n\n**Acceptance (if A).** Start numbers in Settings › Numbers on a Markdown board; a new issue gets the next number on the default branch; on another branch, numbering says why it waits.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","title":"datastores: project numbers on a Markdown board"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793822098,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6206257458"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","a